{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["If a woman conceives — when she becomes pregnant, whether with male or female. If she bears a male, his law shall be thus. And if she bears a female, her law thus and so — he states it in summary fashion and afterwards specifies." "[And she shall be impure] seven days — even if she did not see blood." "As in the days of her menstrual infirmity — as in the days of the separation of her illness set out before us, by seeing impure blood, by seeing childbirth blood." "Menstruant (niddah) — an expression of wandering and separation from her husband." "Her infirmity (davatah) — an expression of illness. As in: לבי דוי."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:43.081612494Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}